<div style="background-color: #e0f2f7; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; font-size: 24px;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 5px; font-size: 16px;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Helping in the Garden</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> These Plants Are from Panama.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: text: Simplify textbook content for peer study groups. communication: Assist classmates in interpreting homework assignments.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can simplify textbook content on gardening topics by miming actions (e.g., mimes 'grow' by pretending to reach up like a plant). Can assist classmates in understanding gardening homework by drawing simple shapes or plants (e.g., drawing a tomato plant and saying, 'These are tomatoes, and this is a tomato plant.'). Can clarify gardening terms for peers with simple gestures (e.g., mimics 'watering a plant' when explaining the verb 'to water').</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f0f8ff;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 34%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts with a "Gardening Mime Challenge." The teacher mimes a gardening action (e.g., 'dig,' 'plant,' 'water,' 'grow,' 'harvest'), and students call out the verb. The teacher then asks, "What do we need for a plant to grow?" eliciting 'sunlight,' 'water,' 'soil,' 'seed.' (5 minutes)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher explains the concept of "helping friends understand." "Sometimes a friend doesn't understand a word or a homework task. We can help them!" The teacher models explaining "water" by miming watering a plant and saying, "To water means to give water to a plant. You use a watering can. See?" (teacher mimes). The teacher also draws a simple tomato plant and says, "This is a tomato plant. These are tomatoes." (7 minutes)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can we use our hands to show a word?" (Yes.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can we draw a picture to help a friend?" (Yes.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is it okay to ask for help?" (Yes.)</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher reinforces that helping each other is important for learning. (3 minutes)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Day 1</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Total: 15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Helping in the Garden".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A simple visual "How-to Guide: Planting a Bean Seed" (e.g., 3-4 illustrated steps). This guide serves as the 'textbook content' or 'homework instructions' for mediation. Each step includes a simple sentence: "1. Dig a small hole in the soil. 2. Put one seed in the hole. 3. Cover the seed with soil. 4. Water the plant every day." (This leverages vocabulary: 'dig,' 'soil,' 'seed,' 'cover,' 'water,' 'plant,' 'every day.')</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Understanding and interpreting simple instructions related to gardening steps, using vocabulary from the theme. Students will also practice phonemic awareness for /t/ in 'tomatoes' (implicitly 'plant') and /g/ in 'grow'. (e.g., when they hear 'dig,' 'grow,' 'plant,' 'water,' 'sun,' 'soil').</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What is this guide about?" (Answer: Planting a seed.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> "Do we water the seed before planting?" (False) "Does the guide say to water the plant every day?" (True)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Sequence matching:</b> The teacher provides scrambled pictures of the steps and asks students to put them in the correct order, referring to the words 'first,' 'second.'</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Teacher emphasizes pronunciation of /t/ in 'plant' and /g/ in 'dig' as students read. (10 minutes)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Day 1</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Total: 10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Mediation.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice mediating simple gardening instructions using miming, drawing, and specific vocabulary (garden, plant, tomato, seed, soil, watering can, grow, water, plant, dig, need, every day, first, second) and grammar (Present simple + 's', Demonstratives, Question forms, discourse markers 'and,' 'but'). Practice phonemic awareness by spelling 'water,' 'sun,' 'soil' aloud.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. <b>Word to Action/Picture Match (Controlled):</b> The teacher displays flashcards with gardening words (e.g., 'dig,' 'seed,' 'grow,' 'water'). Students, in pairs, first mime the word, then draw a quick picture on a mini-whiteboard/paper, and finally say the word, focusing on /t/ and /g/ sounds. They practice spelling 'water,' 'sun,' 'soil.' (e.g., "W-A-T-E-R, water"). (5 minutes)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. <b>Explain and Show (Semi-controlled):</b> In pairs, Student A says a gardening word (e.g., 'soil,' 'watering can,' 'grow'). Student B must explain it using a simple sentence and a gesture or drawing. E.g., Student B: "Soil is where plants grow. It's brown." (points to the floor) or "To grow means to get big." (mimes growing tall like a plant). They use demonstratives: "This is a plant." "These are seeds." (7 minutes)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. <b>"Explain the Step" Mini-Mediation (Pair Interaction):</b> Students work in pairs. Each pair gets one step from the "How-to Guide: Planting a Bean Seed" from Stage 2. Student A reads the step. Student B pretends they don't understand one word (e.g., 'dig,' 'cover,' 'soil'). Student A must explain that word using gestures, a simple drawing, or an example sentence. E.g., "First, dig a small hole." If B doesn't know 'dig,' A mimes digging and says, "To dig means to make a hole in the soil with your hands or a shovel." They also practice asking "Do you understand?" and using 'and' for connecting ideas. (e.g., "You dig a hole and then you put the seed.") (8 minutes)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Day 1</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Total: 20 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Helping in the Garden".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> Paired Mediation Presentation for the "Step-by-Step Planting Guide." Students will apply their mediation skills to clarify parts of their project.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. Students get into pairs. They are given their "Step-by-Step Planting Guide" from Project 2 (created in previous lessons, possibly Lesson 4 writing). Each guide has simple instructions and illustrations.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. In each pair, Student A acts as the "Teacher/Explainer" and Student B acts as the "Learner/Asker."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. Student A presents one step from their guide (e.g., "First, put the soil in the pot"). Student B pretends not to understand a specific word or concept (e.g., "What is 'soil'?" or "What does 'put' mean?").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">4. Student A must clarify the word/concept using:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Miming actions (e.g., mimes 'dig,' 'water,' 'grow').</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Drawing simple pictures on a small whiteboard or paper (e.g., a 'seed,' a 'flower,' 'sunlight,' 'watering can'). They use demonstratives: "This is a seed. These are flowers."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Simple explanations with target vocabulary and grammar (Present Simple + 's': "The plant needs sunlight. It grows tall."; Question forms: "Do you understand?"; Pragmatics: "First, you put soil, and then you add the seed.")</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">5. After 2-3 minutes, students switch roles.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">6. The teacher circulates, offering support and noting effective mediation strategies. (Pronunciation check for /t/ and /g/).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Day 1</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Total: 10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist and Peer Assessment.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each student (in pairs) will present one mediated explanation of a step from their "Step-by-Step Planting Guide" to another pair. One student explains, and the peer confirms understanding. The other pair acts as observers, providing simple peer feedback.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher & Peer):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation of gardening words (e.g., /t/ in 'tomato,' /g/ in 'grow').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effective use of target vocabulary (e.g., 'soil,' 'seed,' 'water,' 'plant,' 'grow,' 'every day,' 'first,' 'second').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of explanation using simple sentences (Present Simple and Demonstratives).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of gestures and/or simple drawings to clarify meaning.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaboration and engagement in helping a peer understand.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete an exit ticket with the following prompts:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. What was one new word you helped your friend understand today? How did you help them?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. What was easy/difficult about explaining things to your friend?</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Day 1</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Total: 10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. "How can I use drawings or gestures to help my family or friends understand new things outside of class?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. "What was my favorite part about helping my friend learn about gardening today?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in engaging students in mediation tasks? The use of miming and drawing was effective for this grade level.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Which students effectively used gestures and drawings to clarify meaning? Some struggled with vocabulary retention when explaining.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for students who found mediation challenging? Provide more sentence frames for explanations or a 'mediation toolkit' with common phrases like "It means..." or "I can show you..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence: This lesson concludes the "These Plants Are from Panama" theme and the "Step-by-Step Planting Guide" project. The next theme will introduce new vocabulary and skills, but the ability to clarify and help peers will remain a valuable skill.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Day 1</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Total: 5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>